[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I produced the deliverable **`churntrainingdbea5e`, version 1**, on the platform (feature view + materialized training dataset v1), reading back through the platform's own read path (`hops td read`).
[agent] **What the interface does correctly**
[agent] - All source data is loaded into feature groups (`transactions` = 658 + 67 late = 725 rows, etc.), including the late export.
[agent] - The **point-in-time join is correct**: for every `(account_id, label_time)` it returns the most-recent feature value at/before `label_time` from each table, joined on `account_id`, and excludes any `event_time` after `label_time`. Verified on multiple rows (e.g. A0002 selects the late-export row `1772323772000` and excludes the two later transactions).
[agent] - `churned` is retained as a column (I did **not** mark it a label, because `hops td read` silently drops label-designated columns from its output).
[agent] **Where the interface falls short of the exact spec — these are the missing capabilities:**
